WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.180
SPEAKER: Your first
project holds the promise

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.340
of the new technology
you're introducing

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.990
to your organization.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.750
If selected and
executed well, it

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.000
can be a showcase
that makes it easier

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.730
to achieve repeated success with
subsequent programs of work.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.340
Every business is competing
in a digital landscape,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.260
irrespective of the industry.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.700
In our modern digital
age, speed is key.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.640
Speed gives the ability to
respond to business challenges

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.350
and opportunities
with digital solutions

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.140
quickly, and at scale.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.860
Your ability to quickly build
and manage APIs with Apigee

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.110
is a key tool for success.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.810
Your first delivery needs
to demonstrate and validate

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.970
to your organization
your ability

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:50.940
to deliver at speed something
that matters to the company.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.180
We call this delivery the
minimum viable business

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.590
outcome.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.590
Your MVBO is an early
win that delivers

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.170
APIs that are core
to your business,

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:06.660
and creates early momentum with
a pathway for repeated success.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.270
Drawing from many years
of working with enterprise

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:12.570
customers to help them with
delivering on their API

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.480
programs, we've seen
patterns that typically

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.490
lead to increased
risk of failure

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.850
or the transformation
program stalling out.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.470
Let's take a look.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:26.260
Typical adoption patterns look
like an S curve, as shown here.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.060
The first part of
the curve is assured.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.330
And after all, you have
the budget and the team

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.460
to get the first
delivery completed.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.880
However, subsequent
adoption can be harder,

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.310
and is often predicated
on the success

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.350
of the early deliveries.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.020
In our experience, customers
who get into production

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.900
quickly with something
core to their business

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.900
are able to maintain and
build stronger momentum

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.000
on the platform,
and are much more

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.210
successful at achieving their
goals of speed and agility

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.250
over the long term.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.620
Careful selection of
your first project

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.510
will help you achieve this.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.570
We'd like to offer three
essential components that

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.940
will improve your
chances for success.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.280
We think about these
three characteristics

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.889
for selecting your
first project--

00:02:10.889 --> 00:02:14.490
ready, rewarding, and relevant.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.460
Let's explore these
characteristics in more detail.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.710
Completing your first
delivery quickly

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.390
with something core
to your business

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.090
gives your program
its strongest start.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.940
Ready means selecting
an MVBO that

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.470
allows for that quick delivery.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:31.600
This means ideally
avoiding items

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.600
that may require significant
backend refactoring that

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.940
might take many
months to complete,

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.510
or avoiding the items
that have dependencies

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.190
on other programs
of work that'll

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.320
take also months to complete.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.020
For example, an API
for a mobile app

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.810
refresh planned
months in the future.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:54.010
Rewarding means ensuring your
MVBO is a strong showcase

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.920
and demonstrates value
to the organization.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.370
Ideally, value here
means recognizable value

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:04.270
to your business leadership that
is a real and tangible impact

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:05.860
to your bottom line.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.380
You may be enabling a new
line of revenue or increasing

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.910
engagement with customers.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.370
The best examples are
measurable with respect

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.470
to the end user
of your business.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:19.030
For example, for retail, this
might be measured in sales.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:21.910
For insurance, it might be
measured in handling time

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.070
for new claims processing.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.830
A great example will also
provide bragging rights

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:27.952
for your sponsor.

00:03:27.952 --> 00:03:29.410
You might want to
deliver something

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.080
that allows your leadership
to widely share the success

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.570
to help bring attention
to the new capability that

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.160
was delivered quickly.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.820
Relevant means that the
initial MVBO is a good use

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.920
case for API management.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.890
This could be reducing
friction for developer adoption

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.800
through better self
service developer portals,

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.560
or measuring usage
through analytics

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.890
that allow traffic to be tied
back to the business drivers.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:57.940
Starting by selecting an MVBO
that is ready, rewarding,

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.790
and relevant will provide
for the strongest start

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:02.440
in a way that sets
your program up

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.780
for sustained momentum
and long term success.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.620
I'd like to share a couple of
real world customer stories

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:13.120
that show how starting with a
good MVBO led to that success

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.570
long term.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.680
The first is a multinational
bank operating out

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.470
of the Middle East, wanting to
demonstrate the ability to get

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.110
new products to market quickly.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.600
Furthermore, their
leadership were looking

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.670
to showcase product innovation.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:30.790
The project team responsible
for deploying Apigee

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:35.350
decided to start with a handful
of pretty straightforward APIs.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:39.250
One was an identity API to
track user authorization,

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.730
an account API with the ability
to set savings interest rates,

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:45.070
and a wrapper for
the Apple Watch API

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.680
that could pull step
count information.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.950
The team was able to launch
a new savings account that

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.980
linked to your Apple Watch such
that the further you walked,

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.930
the higher your interest rate.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.160
Pretty nice, huh?

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.500
Importantly, they were able
to launch this new product

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:03.010
in just 12 weeks, way
faster than the typical time

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:05.140
frames for product
development for this bank.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.090
That's even better.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.850
Our second example
comes from retail.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.490
This well-established
brick and mortar retailer

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.630
was looking to defend against
online only new market entrants

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.050
by successfully launching
their own e-commerce store.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.690
Instead of trying to do
too much at the start,

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.580
they began with
simple use cases that

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.020
were core to enabling
the e-commerce business,

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.800
including inventory and
customer information.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.470
After securing
success and confidence

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.210
by delivering on
these early use cases,

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.820
they found other
business leaders

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.640
in the organization
coming to the API team

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.470
to create an access
similar tools.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:46.050
Over time, this
led to a buildout

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.930
of a full set of capabilities
towards establishing

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:52.650
a federated ecosystem where
distributed sellers could

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.990
do business with customers
via the API powered

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.180
e-commerce platform.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.400
Best of luck with
your first project.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.070
If you want more
information, please check out

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.650
the community for
ebooks, articles,

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.700
and other related topics.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:08.780
Thank you for watching.

